{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Behemoth</b> — the name of a great animal; there is none in the inhabited world greater than it. The sense of \"with you\" is because it was on dry land, for afterward he mentions Leviathan, which is in the sea. Some say: the sense of \"with you\" is that behemoth were born on a single day with the first man, and this is the way of derash." "<b>It eats grass like an ox</b> — because of this the commentators say: that it is the elephant, but it is not a conclusive proof." "<b>Grass</b> — vegetation, as in: \"who causes grass to grow on the mountains\" (Psalms 147:8)."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:05:30.043645576Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}